config.ws.category.difficulty.tooltip=Configure wizardry's difficulty
config.ws.title.difficulty=Difficulty Settings
config.ws.subtitle.difficulty=Settings that affect the mod's difficulty.
config.ws.unfocused_search_bars=Whether to autofocus search bar in Arcane Workbench and lectern
config.ws.discovery_mode=Discovery Mode
config.ws.discovery_mode.tooltip=For those who like a sense of mystery! When enabled, spells you haven't cast yet will be unreadable until you cast them (on a per-world basis). Has no effect when in creative mode. Spells of identification will be unobtainable in survival mode if this is disabled.
config.ws.legacy_wand_levelling=Legacy Wand Levelling
config.ws.legacy_wand_levelling.tooltip=Controls whether wands are required to gain progression before they can be upgraded to the next tier. Enable this option to revert to the pre-4.2 system, which only requires tomes of arcana. Wands will still gain progression silently when this is enabled, so if you go back to the new system you won't lose any progress.
config.ws.legacy_wand_levelling.true=Yes - I liked it how it was!
config.ws.legacy_wand_levelling.false=No - Level me up!
config.ws.friendly_fire=Friendly Fire
config.ws.friendly_fire.tooltip=Controls which creatures may be damaged by your magic when allied to you. Your spells will not target your allies or creatures summoned/owned by them regardless of this setting, but this setting makes them completely immune if disabled.
config.ws.passive_mobs_are_allies=Passive Mobs Are Allies
config.ws.passive_mobs_are_allies.tooltip=Whether all passive mobs should count as allies, i.e. they should not be damaged indirectly by spells. Tamed mobs always count as allies.
config.ws.passive_mobs_are_allies.true=Yes - don't hurt the animals!
config.ws.passive_mobs_are_allies.false=No - I like my steak lightning-grilled!
config.ws.minion_revenge_targeting=Minion Revenge Targeting
config.ws.minion_revenge_targeting.tooltip=Whether summoned creatures can revenge-attack players or creatures that they would not otherwise be able to attack.
config.ws.minion_revenge_targeting.true=Yes - I'd never hurt them!
config.ws.minion_revenge_targeting.false=No - they must always obey me!
config.ws.forfeit_chance=Forfeit Chance
config.ws.forfeit_chance.tooltip=The chance to 'misread' an undiscovered spell and trigger a forfeit instead. Setting this to 0 effectively disables the forfeit mechanic. Has no effect if discovery mode is disabled.
config.ws.progression_requirements=Progression Requirements
config.ws.progression_requirements.tooltip=The progression required to upgrade a wand to each tier (apprentice, advanced and master respectively).
config.ws.tier_max_charges=Tier Maximum Charges
config.ws.tier_max_charges.tooltip=Maximum mana each tier can store (novice, apprentice, advanced, master respectively).
config.ws.tier_upgrade_limits=Tier Upgrade Limits
config.ws.tier_upgrade_limits.tooltip=Maximum number of upgrades each tier can have (novice, apprentice, advanced, master respectively).
config.ws.novice_max_charge=Novice Maximum Charge
config.ws.novice_max_charge.tooltip=Maximum mana a novice wand can store.
config.ws.apprentice_max_charge=Apprentice Maximum Charge
config.ws.apprentice_max_charge.tooltip=Maximum mana an apprentice wand can store.
config.ws.advanced_max_charge=Advanced Maximum Charge
config.ws.advanced_max_charge.tooltip=Maximum mana an advanced wand can store.
config.ws.master_max_charge=Master Maximum Charge
config.ws.master_max_charge.tooltip=Maximum mana a master wand can store.
config.ws.novice_upgrade_limit=Novice Upgrade Limit
config.ws.novice_upgrade_limit.tooltip=Maximum number of upgrades a novice wand can have.
config.ws.apprentice_upgrade_limit=Apprentice Upgrade Limit
config.ws.apprentice_upgrade_limit.tooltip=Maximum number of upgrades an apprentice wand can have.
config.ws.advanced_upgrade_limit=Advanced Upgrade Limit
config.ws.advanced_upgrade_limit.tooltip=Maximum number of upgrades an advanced wand can have.
config.ws.master_upgrade_limit=Master Upgrade Limit
config.ws.master_upgrade_limit.tooltip=Maximum number of upgrades a master wand can have.
config.ws.condenser_amount_multiplier=Condenser Amount Multiplier
config.ws.condenser_amount_multiplier.tooltip=Multiplier for condenser upgrade mana regeneration amount. Higher values make condensers more effective.
config.ws.flesh_spells_cause_slowness=Flesh Spells Cause Slowness
config.ws.flesh_spells_cause_slowness.tooltip=Whether flesh spells (DiamondFlesh, IronFlesh, OakFlesh) apply slowness. When disabled, these spells only provide their defensive benefits without movement penalty.
config.ws.flesh_spells_cause_slowness.true=Yes - flesh spells slow you down
config.ws.flesh_spells_cause_slowness.false=No - flesh spells don't slow you down
config.ws.diamond_flesh_armor_bonus=DiamondFlesh Armor Bonus
config.ws.diamond_flesh_armor_bonus.tooltip=Armor bonus provided by the DiamondFlesh spell.
config.ws.diamond_flesh_armor_toughness_bonus=DiamondFlesh Armor Toughness Bonus
config.ws.diamond_flesh_armor_toughness_bonus.tooltip=Armor toughness bonus provided by the DiamondFlesh spell.
config.ws.iron_flesh_armor_bonus=IronFlesh Armor Bonus
config.ws.iron_flesh_armor_bonus.tooltip=Armor bonus provided by the IronFlesh spell.
config.ws.oak_flesh_armor_bonus=OakFlesh Armor Bonus
config.ws.oak_flesh_armor_bonus.tooltip=Armor bonus provided by the OakFlesh spell.
config.ws.oak_flesh_health_bonus=OakFlesh Health Bonus
config.ws.oak_flesh_health_bonus.tooltip=Health bonus provided by the OakFlesh spell (as a multiplier, e.g., 0.2 = 20% increase).
config.ws.player_damage_scaling=Player Damage Scaling Factor
config.ws.player_damage_scaling.tooltip=Global damage scaling factor for the damage dealt by players casting spells, relative to 1.
config.ws.npc_damage_scaling=NPC Damage Scaling Factor
config.ws.npc_damage_scaling.tooltip=Global damage scaling factor for the damage dealt by NPCs casting spells, relative to 1.
config.ws.evil_wizard_spawn_rate=Evil Wizard Spawn Rate
config.ws.evil_wizard_spawn_rate.tooltip=Spawn rate for naturally-spawned evil wizards; higher numbers mean more evil wizards will spawn. 5 is equivalent to witches, 100 is equivalent to zombies, skeletons and creepers. Set to 0 to disable evil wizard spawning entirely.
config.ws.ice_wraith_spawn_rate=Ice Wraith Spawn Rate
config.ws.ice_wraith_spawn_rate.tooltip=Spawn rate for naturally-spawned ice wraiths; higher numbers mean more ice wraiths will spawn. 5 is equivalent to witches, 100 is equivalent to zombies, skeletons and creepers. Set to 0 to disable ice wraith spawning entirely.
config.ws.lightning_wraith_spawn_rate=Lightning Wraith Spawn Rate
config.ws.lightning_wraith_spawn_rate.tooltip=Spawn rate for naturally-spawned lightning wraiths; higher numbers mean more lightning wraiths will spawn. 5 is equivalent to witches, 100 is equivalent to zombies, skeletons and creepers. Set to 0 to disable lightning wraith spawning entirely.
config.ws.category.tweaks=Tweaks Settings
config.ws.category.tweaks.tooltip=Tweak wizardry's behaviour
config.ws.title.tweaks=Tweaks Settings
config.ws.subtitle.tweaks=Assorted settings for tweaking the mod's behaviour.
config.ws.replace_vanilla_fireballs=Replace Vanilla Fireballs
config.ws.replace_vanilla_fireballs.tooltip=Whether to replace Minecraft's own fireballs with wizardry fireballs. If this is disabled, only wizardry spells will use the custom fireballs.
config.ws.replace_vanilla_fireballs.true=Yes - give me FIRE!
config.ws.replace_vanilla_fireballs.false=No - blazes are mean enough
config.ws.replace_vanilla_fall_damage=Replace Vanilla Fall Damage
config.ws.replace_vanilla_fall_damage.tooltip=Whether to replace Minecraft's distance-based fall damage calculation with an equivalent, velocity-based one. This is done such that mobs in freefall will take exactly the same damage as normal, so it will not break falling-based mob farms. Disable this if you experience falling-related weirdness! If this is disabled, some spells revert to a more simplistic method of resetting the player's fall damage in certain cases.
config.ws.replace_vanilla_fall_damage.true=Yes - it's parkour time
config.ws.replace_vanilla_fall_damage.false=No - break my legs normally
config.ws.spell_book_colors_require_charm=Spell Book Colors Require Archivist's Eyeglass
config.ws.spell_book_colors_require_charm.tooltip=Whether to require the Archivist's Eyeglass charm artifact to see colored spell book bookmarks.
config.ws.spell_book_colors_require_charm.true=Yes - I want to see the colours only if the charm is worn
config.ws.spell_book_colors_require_charm.false=No - I want to see the colours all the time
config.ws.blindness_tweak=Blindness Tweak
config.ws.blindness_tweak.tooltip=Whether to tweak the blindness effect to reduce follow distance when used on non-players. This automatically disables itself in favour of Potion Core's implementation if installed.
config.ws.mob_loot_table_whitelist=Mob Loot Table Whitelist
config.ws.mob_loot_table_whitelist.tooltip=Whitelist for loot tables to inject additional mob drops (as specified in loot_tables/entities/mob_additions.json) into. Wizardry makes a best guess as to which loot tables belong to hostile mobs, but this may not always be correct or appropriate; add loot table locations (not entity IDs) to this list to manually include them.
config.ws.mob_loot_table_blacklist=Mob Loot Table Blacklist
config.ws.mob_loot_table_blacklist.tooltip=Blacklist for loot tables to inject additional mob drops (as specified in loot_tables/entities/mob_additions.json) into. Wizardry makes a best guess as to which loot tables belong to hostile mobs, but this may not always be correct or appropriate; add loot table locations (not entity IDs) to this list to manually exclude them.
config.ws.inject_mob_drops=Allow Wizardry Mob Loot
config.ws.inject_mob_drops.tooltip=Whether to inject Wizardry loot to mobs, based on the loot table 'Mob Loot Table Whitelist' / 'Mob Loot Table Blacklist' settings. If disabled, the lists won't have any effect!
config.ws.mob_spawn_dimensions=Mob Spawning Dimensions
config.ws.mob_spawn_dimensions.tooltip=List of ids of dimensions in which wizardry's hostile mobs can spawn.
config.ws.mob_spawn_biome_blacklist=Mob Spawning Biome Blacklist
config.ws.mob_spawn_biome_blaclist.tooltip=List of names of biomes in which wizardry's hostile mobs cannot spawn. Biome names are not case-sensitive. For mod biomes, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. biomesoplenty\:mystic_grove).
config.ws.summoned_creature_targets_whitelist=Summoned Creature Target Whitelist
config.ws.summoned_creature_targets_whitelist.tooltip=List of names of entities which summoned creatures and wizards are allowed to attack, in addition to the defaults. Add mod creatures to this list if you want summoned creatures to attack them and they aren't already doing so. Entity names are not case sensitive. For mod entities, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. ws:wizard).
config.ws.summoned_creature_targets_blacklist=Summoned Creature Target Blacklist
config.ws.summoned_creature_targets_blacklist.tooltip=List of names of entities which summoned creatures and wizards are specifically not allowed to attack, overriding the defaults and the whitelist. Add creatures to this list if allowing them to be attacked causes problems or is too destructive (removing creepers from this list is done at your own risk!). Entity names are not case sensitive. For mod entities, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. ws:wizard).
config.ws.mind_control_targets_blacklist=Mind Control Targets Blacklist
config.ws.mind_control_targets_blacklist.tooltip=List of names of entities which cannot be mind controlled, in addition to the defaults. Add creatures to this list if allowing them to be mind-controlled causes problems or could be exploited. Entity names are not case sensitive. For mod entities, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. ws:wizard).
config.ws.pocket_furnace_item_blacklist=Pocket Furnace Item Blacklist
config.ws.pocket_furnace_item_blacklist.tooltip=List of registry names of blocks or items which cannot be smelted by the pocket furnace spell, in addition to armour, tools and weapons. Block/item names are not case sensitive. For mod items, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. ws:crystal_ore).
config.ws.divination_ore_whitelist=Divination Ore Whitelist
config.ws.divination_ore_whitelist.tooltip=List of registry names of ore blocks which can be detected by the divination spell. Block names are not case sensitive. For mod blocks, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. ws:crystal_ore).
config.ws.sword_item_whitelist=Sword Item Whitelist
config.ws.sword_item_whitelist.tooltip=List of registry names of items which should count as swords for imbuement spells. Most swords should work automatically, but those that don't can be added manually here. Item names are not case sensitive. For mod items, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. tconstruct:broadsword).
config.ws.bow_item_whitelist=Bow Item Whitelist
config.ws.bow_item_whitelist.tooltip=List of registry names of items which should count as bows for imbuement spells. Most bows should work automatically, but those that don't can be added manually here. Item names are not case sensitive. For mod items, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. tconstruct:shortbow).
config.ws.bookshelf_blocks=Bookshelf Blocks
config.ws.bookshelf_blocks.tooltip=List of registry names of blocks that count as bookshelves for the arcane workbench and lectern. Block names are not case sensitive. For mod blocks, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. ws:oak_bookshelf).
config.ws.book_items=Book Items
config.ws.book_items.tooltip=List of registry names of items which can be placed in a bookshelf, in addition to the defaults. Item names are not case sensitive. For mod items, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. thaumcraft:thaumonomicon).
config.ws.bookshelf_search_radius=Bookshelf Search Radius
config.ws.bookshelf_search_radius.tooltip=The maximum number of blocks a bookshelf can be from an arcane workbench or lectern to be able to link to it.
config.ws.currency_items=Currency Items
config.ws.currency_items.tooltip=List of registry names of items which wizard trades can use as currency (in the first slot; the second slot is unaffected). Each entry in this list should consist of an item registry name, followed by a single space, then an integer which defines the 'value' of the item. Higher values mean fewer of that currency item are required for a given trade.
config.ws.category.worldgen=World Generation Settings
config.ws.category.worldgen.tooltip=Configure wizardry's world generation features
config.ws.title.worldgen=World Generation Settings
config.ws.subtitle.worldgen=Settings that affect world generation.
config.ws.fast_worldgen=Structure Generation
config.ws.fast_worldgen.tooltip=Controls which algorithm wizardry uses for structure generation. Fancy worldgen prevents structures on cliffs, in caves and intersecting other structures, and cleans up floating trees after generating. Fast worldgen sacrifices these improvements, potentially resulting in faster world generation. Performance improvement will vary depending on your setup. This option will affect randomisation; for any given seed, structures will not be the same as when it is turned off.
config.ws.fast_worldgen.true=Fast
config.ws.fast_worldgen.false=Fancy
config.ws.tower_dimensions=Tower Dimensions
config.ws.tower_dimensions.tooltip=List of ids of dimensions in which wizard towers will generate. Remove all dimensions to disable wizard towers completely.
config.ws.tower_rarity=Tower Rarity
config.ws.tower_rarity.tooltip=Rarity of wizard towers. 1 in this many chunks will contain a wizard tower, meaning higher numbers are rarer.
config.ws.evil_wizard_chance=Evil Wizard Chance
config.ws.evil_wizard_chance.tooltip=The chance for wizard towers to generate with an evil wizard and chest inside, instead of a friendly wizard.
config.ws.tower_files=Tower Structure Files
config.ws.tower_files.tooltip=List of structure file locations for wizard towers without loot chests. One of these files will be randomly selected each time a wizard tower is generated. File locations are of the format [mod id]\:[filename], which refers to the file assets/[mod id]/structures/[filename].nbt. Duplicate entries are permitted, allowing for simple weighting without duplicating the structure files themselves. This list should not be empty; to disable wizard towers, use the tower dimensions setting.
config.ws.tower_with_chest_files=Tower With Chest Structure Files
config.ws.tower_with_chest_files.tooltip=List of structure file locations for wizard towers with loot chests. One of these files will be randomly selected each time a wizard tower is generated. File locations are of the format [mod id]\:[filename], which refers to the file assets/[mod id]/structures/[filename].nbt. Duplicate entries are permitted, allowing for simple weighting without duplicating the structure files themselves. This list should not be empty; to disable wizard towers, use the tower dimensions setting.
config.ws.obelisk_dimensions=Obelisk Dimensions
config.ws.obelisk_dimensions.tooltip=List of ids of dimensions in which obelisks will generate. Remove all dimensions to disable obelisks completely.
config.ws.obelisk_rarity=Obelisk Rarity
config.ws.obelisk_rarity.tooltip=Rarity of obelisks. 1 in this many chunks will contain an obelisk, meaning higher numbers are rarer.
config.ws.obelisk_files=Obelisk Structure Files
config.ws.obelisk_files.tooltip=List of structure file locations for obelisks. One of these files will be randomly selected each time an obelisk is generated. File locations are of the format [mod id]\:[filename], which refers to the file assets/[mod id]/structures/[filename].nbt. Duplicate entries are permitted, allowing for simple weighting without duplicating the structure files themselves. This list should not be empty; to disable obelisks, use the obelisk dimensions setting.
config.ws.shrine_dimensions=Shrine Dimensions
config.ws.shrine_dimensions.tooltip=List of ids of dimensions in which shrines will generate. Remove all dimensions to disable shrines completely.
config.ws.shrine_rarity=Shrine Rarity
config.ws.shrine_rarity.tooltip=Rarity of shrines. 1 in this many chunks will contain a shrine, meaning higher numbers are rarer.
config.ws.shrine_files=Shrine Structure Files
config.ws.shrine_files.tooltip=List of structure file locations for shrines. One of these files will be randomly selected each time a shrine is generated. File locations are of the format [mod id]\:[filename], which refers to the file assets/[mod id]/structures/[filename].nbt. Duplicate entries are permitted, allowing for simple weighting without duplicating the structure files themselves. This list should not be empty; to disable shrines, use the shrine dimensions setting.
config.ws.library_dimensions=Library Ruin Dimensions
config.ws.library_dimensions.tooltip=List of ids of dimensions in which library ruins will generate. Remove all dimensions to disable library ruins completely.
config.ws.library_rarity=Library Ruin Rarity
config.ws.library_rarity.tooltip=Rarity of library ruins. 1 in this many chunks will contain a shrine, meaning higher numbers are rarer.
config.ws.library_files=Library Ruin Structure Files
config.ws.library_files.tooltip=List of structure file locations for surface library ruins. One of these files will be randomly selected each time a library ruin is generated. File locations are of the format [mod id]\:[filename], which refers to the file assets/[mod id]/structures/[filename].nbt. Duplicate entries are permitted, allowing for simple weighting without duplicating the structure files themselves. This list should not be empty; to disable library ruins, use the library ruin dimensions setting.
config.ws.underground_library_files=Underground Library Ruin Structure Files
config.ws.underground_library_files.tooltip=List of structure file locations for underground library ruins. One of these files will be randomly selected each time a library ruin is generated. File locations are of the format [mod id]\:[filename], which refers to the file assets/[mod id]/structures/[filename].nbt. Duplicate entries are permitted, allowing for simple weighting without duplicating the structure files themselves. This list should not be empty; to disable library ruins, use the library ruin dimensions setting.
config.ws.tree_blocks=Tree Blocks
config.ws.tree_blocks.tooltip=List of registry names of blocks which can be overwritten by wizardry's structure generators, affecting both fast and fancy structure generation. Most tree blocks and other foliage should work automatically, but those that don't can be added manually here. Block names are not case sensitive. For mod blocks, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. dynamictrees:oakbranch).
config.ws.ore_dimensions=Ore Dimensions
config.ws.ore_dimensions.tooltip=List of ids of dimensions in which crystal ore will generate. Note that removing the overworld (id 0) from this list will make the mod VERY difficult to play!
config.ws.flower_dimensions=Flower Dimensions
config.ws.flower_dimensions.tooltip=List of ids of dimensions in which crystal flowers will generate.
config.ws.loot_injection_locations=Loot Injection Locations
config.ws.loot_injection_locations.tooltip=List of loot tables to inject wizardry loot (as specified in loot_tables/chests/dungeon_additions.json) into.
config.ws.category.client=Client Settings
config.ws.category.client.tooltip=Configure wizardry's display and controls
config.ws.title.client=Client Settings
config.ws.subtitle.client=Client-side settings that only affect the local minecraft game.
config.ws.shift_scrolling=Shift-scrolling
config.ws.shift_scrolling.tooltip=Whether you can switch between spells on a wand by scrolling with the mouse wheel while sneaking. Note that this will only affect you; other players connected to the same server obey their own settings.
config.ws.reverse_scroll_direction=Scroll Direction
config.ws.reverse_scroll_direction.tooltip=The scroll direction used to switch between spells on a wand while sneaking.
config.ws.reverse_scroll_direction.true=Reversed
config.ws.reverse_scroll_direction.false=Normal
config.ws.show_spell_hud=Spell HUD
config.ws.show_spell_hud.tooltip=Whether to show the spell HUD in the corner of the screen when holding a wand.
config.ws.show_spell_hud.true=Shown
config.ws.show_spell_hud.false=Hidden
config.ws.show_charge_meter=Spell Charge Meter
config.ws.show_charge_meter.tooltip=Whether to show the spell charge-up meter around the crosshairs when charging up a spell.
config.ws.show_charge_meter.true=Shown
config.ws.show_charge_meter.false=Hidden
config.ws.spell_hud_position=Spell HUD Position
config.ws.spell_hud_position.tooltip=The position of the spell HUD.
config.ws.spell_hud_skin=Spell HUD Skin
config.ws.spell_hud_skin.tooltip=Change the look of the spell HUD...
config.ws.spell_hud_skin.preview=Preview
config.ws.handbook_progression=Handbook Progression
config.ws.handbook_progression.tooltip=When enabled, to help guide players through the mod, sections of The Wizard's Handbook are unlocked when a player gains the advancement that triggers them, and are hidden otherwise. When disabled, the entire handbook is readable regardless of advancement progress. The entire handbook is always readable in creative mode.
config.ws.handbook_progression.true=Yes - teach me, Sensei!
config.ws.handbook_progression.false=No - I know what I'm doing
config.ws.books_pause_game=Books Pause Game
config.ws.books_pause_game.tooltip=Whether opening any of wizardry's books pauses the game in singleplayer. Has no effect on servers or LAN worlds.
config.ws.books_pause_game.true=Yes - I don't want any distractions!
config.ws.books_pause_game.false=No - I read to pass the time
config.ws.summoned_creature_names=Summoned Creature Names
config.ws.summoned_creature_names.tooltip=Controls whether summoned creatures' names and owners are displayed above their heads.
config.ws.summoned_creature_names.true=Shown
config.ws.summoned_creature_names.false=Hidden
config.ws.use_shaders=Use Custom Shaders
config.ws.use_shaders.tooltip=Whether to use custom shaders for certain spells. These use the vanilla shader system (like mob spectating shaders) and shouldn't have much of an effect on performance in most cases, but they may conflict with other shaders.
config.ws.use_shaders.true=Yes - gimme those sweet shaders!
config.ws.use_shaders.false=No - I'm running this on a potato
config.ws.screen_shake=Screen Shake
config.ws.screen_shake.tooltip=Whether to use the screen shake effect for certain spells.
config.ws.blink_effect=Blink Effect
config.ws.blink_effect.tooltip=Whether to use the screen blink effect for teleportation spells.
config.ws.spellcasting_animations=Spellcasting Animations
config.ws.spellcasting_animations.tooltip=Whether to use custom animations for players casting spells. Disable this option if it conflicts with other mods that add player animations.
config.ws.donation_perk_element=Donation Perk Element
config.ws.donation_perk_element.tooltip=The element of the flying companion orb rendered on donor and contributor players, leave empty to disable the effect. If you're one of them, this setting will change how all players see you (if not, it won't do anything).
config.ws.category.commands=Command Settings
config.ws.category.commands.tooltip=Configure wizardry's commands
config.ws.title.commands=Command Settings
config.ws.subtitle.commands=Settings for the commands added by Wizardry.
config.ws.cast_command_multiplier_limit=Cast Command Multiplier Limit
config.ws.cast_command_multiplier_limit.tooltip=Upper limit for the multipliers passed into the /cast command. This is here to stop players from accidentally breaking a world/server. Large blast mutipliers can cause extreme lag - you have been warned!
config.ws.cast_command_name=Cast Spell Command Name
config.ws.cast_command_name.tooltip=The name of the /cast command. This is what you type directly after the /; for example if this was set to 'magic' then instead of typing /cast you would type /magic instead.
config.ws.discoverspell_command_name=Discover Spell Command Name
config.ws.discoverspell_command_name.tooltip=The name of the /discoverspell command. This is what you type directly after the /; for example if this was set to 'magic' then instead of typing /discoverspell you would type /magic instead.
config.ws.ally_command_name=Set Ally Command Name
config.ws.ally_command_name.tooltip=The name of the /ally command. This is what you type directly after the /; for example if this was set to 'magic' then instead of typing /ally you would type /magic instead.
config.ws.allies_command_name=View Allies Command Name
config.ws.allies_command_name.tooltip=The name of the /allies command. This is what you type directly after the /; for example if this was set to 'magic' then instead of typing /allies you would type /magic instead.
config.ws.category.resistances=Resistance Configuration
config.ws.category.resistances.tooltip=Configure which mobs are immune to different types of magic
config.ws.title.resistances=Resistance Configuration
config.ws.subtitle.resistances=Settings which allow entities to be made immune to certain types of magic.
config.ws.mobs_immune_to_fire=Mobs Immune To Fire
config.ws.mobs_immune_to_fire.tooltip=List of names of entities that are immune to fire, in addition to the defaults. Add mod creatures to this list if you want them to be immune to fire magic and they aren't already. Entity names are not case sensitive. For mod entities, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. ws:wizard).
config.ws.mobs_immune_to_ice=Mobs Immune To Ice
config.ws.mobs_immune_to_ice.tooltip=List of names of entities that are immune to ice, in addition to the defaults. Add mod creatures to this list if you want them to be immune to ice magic and they aren't already. Entity names are not case sensitive. For mod entities, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. ws:wizard).
config.ws.mobs_immune_to_lightning=Mobs Immune To Lightning
config.ws.mobs_immune_to_lightning.tooltip=List of names of entities that are immune to lightning, in addition to the defaults. Add mod creatures to this list if you want them to be immune to lightning magic and they aren't already. Entity names are not case sensitive. For mod entities, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. ws:wizard).
config.ws.mobs_immune_to_magic=Mobs Immune To Magic
config.ws.mobs_immune_to_magic.tooltip=List of names of entities that are immune to magic, in addition to the defaults. Add mod creatures to this list if you want them to be immune to magic damage and they aren't already. Entity names are not case sensitive. For mod entities, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. ws:wizard).
config.ws.mobs_immune_to_wither=Mobs Immune To Wither
config.ws.mobs_immune_to_wither.tooltip=List of names of entities that are immune to wither effects, in addition to the defaults. Add mod creatures to this list if you want them to be immune to withering magic and they aren't already. Entity names are not case sensitive. For mod entities, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. ws:wizard).
config.ws.mobs_immune_to_poison=Mobs Immune To Poison
config.ws.mobs_immune_to_poison.tooltip=List of names of entities that are immune to poison, in addition to the defaults. Add mod creatures to this list if you want them to be immune to poison magic and they aren't already. Entity names are not case sensitive. For mod entities, prefix with the mod ID (e.g. ws:wizard).
config.ws.category.compatibility=Mod Compatibility Settings
config.ws.category.compatibility.tooltip=Configure how wizardry interacts with other mods
config.ws.title.compatibility=Mod Compatibility Settings
config.ws.subtitle.compatibility=Settings that affect how wizardry interacts with other mods
config.ws.damage_source_blacklist=Damage Source Blacklist
